{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508196-playing-with-assets","id":1508196,"title":"Playing with Assets","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-12T14:15:09-07:00","id":1508196,"title":"Playing with Assets","content":"In our party we like to play with assets, it give a &quot;personal touch&quot; to the character of each pc. During our game we wondered a few time how to let pc develop some more. Obviously an assets like &quot;resistance to silver&quot; would not be given except as an exceptionnal reward from a spirit, but some other like ambidextrous could be obtain through in game hard training.<br /> <br /> The question is would it cost xp or obtain after some roll? <br /> For the ambidextrous assets i thought about extended roll of dex + athletics difficulty 7/8 and get 10 success would be appropriate","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T16:42:33-07:00","id":1508210,"title":"","content":"Are you talking about Merits?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-13T01:49:13-07:00","id":1508258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508196-playing-with-assets?p=1508210#post1508210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you talking about Merits?</div> </div> </div> </div>The translation is still a bit difficult for me but it looks like it, the list p.473 of W20 and p.487 of V20","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-13T14:19:54-07:00","id":1508299,"title":"","content":"In general I'd not treat Merits or Flaws as something that's bought for experience (or backgrounds for that matter). They can be a result of roleplay, but it's the ST's prerrogative how they raise and what the requirements are. I tend to prefer not having Merits and Flaws in chargen as they tend towards complicating things unnecessarily, but if they really help out with a character type I can see that as reasonable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-13T16:31:45-07:00","id":1508307,"title":"","content":"I'm personally not against Merits in charge, flaws are a bit more problematic. The system as it exists is too open to min-maxing nab the flaws least relevant to your area of expertise are least likely to come up and enjoy the bonus freebies! Yeah the ST is meant to stop that, but it's rarely obvious how much impact a flash will actually have.<br /> <br /> I much prefer flaws as another source of Willpower. Let them cause you a setback and get a reward, going with a carrot rather than a stick. The one exception to that is a Metis flaw, they're generally pretty broad and give you full regen in all forms.<br /> <br /> As to Merits, I'm mostly fine with them. They're rarely necessary, but one or two can round out a character. I'd just straight up charge XP for anybody who wants to earn them in play like CofD does, but I'm also one of those 'if you've not spent the XP it can't go on your sheet, if it comes off your sheet you get the XP back' people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-13T17:40:17-07:00","id":1508309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508196-playing-with-assets?p=1508307#post1508307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm personally not against Merits in charge, flaws are a bit more problematic. The system as it exists is too open to min-maxing nab the flaws least relevant to your area of expertise are least likely to come up and enjoy the bonus freebies! Yeah the ST is meant to stop that, but it's rarely obvious how much impact a flash will actually have.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly, WoD is weirdly the best place for this. Story's are full of hypercompetent characters who're crippled in areas outside their expertise(for examples: see the five-man-band trope, the smart guy is typically physically weak or crippled, the big guy typically has a learning disorder or speech impediment, etc.)<br /> <br /> Min-maxing itself isn't a problem, this is a game meant for fun after all. Let people play the character they want, just make sure they don't get in the way of other character's having the spotlight when it's their turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}